New images of dummy models offer an early look at the purported designs of the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-air/">iPhone Air</a> 2 and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18/">iPhone 18</a>, showing a new dual rear camera arrangement for the Air and a largely unchanged appearance for the standard model.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/iphone-air-2-and-iphone-18-dummy-models.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1078509" /><br/>
In a new post on X, leaker <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/sonny-dickson/">Sonny Dickson</a> highlights the &zwnj;iPhone Air&zwnj;'s move from one rear camera to two as the biggest change. The standard &zwnj;iPhone 18&zwnj;, he says, retains a design similar to the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17/">iPhone 17</a>. A second image shows the fronts of the mockups.<br/>
<br/>
The &zwnj;iPhone Air&zwnj; 2 mockup places both lenses horizontally toward the left side of its raised camera plateau, with the microphone and flash to their right. The plateau continues to stretch across most of the device's width. By comparison, the standard &zwnj;iPhone 18&zwnj; dummy has two vertically stacked lenses within a smaller, pill-shaped camera bump.<br/>
<br/>
