Dummy models are nonfunctional replicas typically produced using leaked dimensions and design information from Apple's supply chain. Accessory manufacturers use them to develop and test cases before the actual devices are available, allowing products to be ready around launch. This preparation makes dummy models a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/09/05/case-makers-reveal-iphone-17-designs/">recurring source of early design previews</a>, particularly for camera layouts, button placement, and overall proportions.<br/>
<br/>
The second rear camera has been a consistent &zwnj;iPhone Air&zwnj; 2 rumor for more than a year. <em>The Information</em> <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/11/11/report-delayed-iphone-air-2-second-camera/">reported in November 2025</a> that Apple was considering the addition as part of a redesign, with subsequent reports continuing to point to a dual-camera system.<br/>
<br/>
The first-generation &zwnj;iPhone Air&zwnj; has a single 48-megapixel Fusion camera. Analyst Jeff Pu later predicted that its successor would <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/31/iphone-air-2-five-new-features-rumored/">gain a 48-megapixel Ultra Wide camera</a>, adding a wider field of view to the device's photography capabilities.<br/>
<br/>
Beyond the additional camera, Pu <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/31/iphone-air-2-five-new-features-rumored/">expects</a> the next &zwnj;iPhone Air&zwnj; to feature an A20 Pro chip, a slightly smaller <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/dynamic-island/">Dynamic Island</a>, Apple's C2 modem, and an N2 wireless networking chip, while retaining a 6.5-inch display and 12GB of RAM. <em>The Information</em> previously reported that Apple was <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/11/10/next-generation-iphone-air-delayed/">working on a larger battery, reduced weight, and vapor chamber cooling</a> for the second-generation model.<br/>
<br/>
The standard &zwnj;iPhone 18&zwnj; is expected to adopt the A20 chip and C2 modem, and could also gain a smaller &zwnj;Dynamic Island&zwnj; like the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a>. <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/ming-chi-kuo/">Ming-Chi Kuo</a> expects <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/26/iphone-18-9gb-ram/">9GB of memory</a>, up from the &zwnj;iPhone 17&zwnj;'s 8GB, while Pu predicts 12GB.<br/>
<br/>
